nr-office-pdf-jpx-codestream: what the lead applies after the wave

1. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/codec/mod.rs (created by nr-office-pdf-jbig2-generic): add the line
       pub mod jpx;
   next to its other `pub mod` lines (alphabetical: after `pub mod jbig2;` and before any later module). The module is
   native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/codec/jpx/mod.rs with boxes.rs, markers.rs, packets.rs and tiles.rs beside it.
   If codec/mod.rs does not exist when the wave is applied, create it containing only `pub mod jpx;` and add
   `pub mod codec;` to native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/lib.rs (before `pub mod codec_glue;`) unless the
   jbig2-generic fragment already does.

2. native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/Cargo.toml, section [dev-dependencies] (after `flate2 = { workspace = true }`), the
   tests/jpx_codestream.rs test reads the fixtures through the test kit and parses expected.json:
       mixdog-testkit = { workspace = true }
       serde_json = { workspace = true }
   native/core/Cargo.lock: the `mixdog-pdf` package entry gains "mixdog-testkit" and "serde_json" in its dependency
   list (both are already locked for other members; no new crate). mixdog-workspace-hack needs nothing new.

