4. native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json (the index): run
       node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index
   so the new set native/core/fixtures/office-jpx (MANIFEST.json written by record-office-jpx.mjs with fileCount,
   totalBytes and per-file sha256) is listed. The recorder writes the set by itself and needs no --tree: it is built
   from pdfjs-dist in node_modules (the reference decoder) and has no product tree to record an identity for.

5. SERVICE_PENDING in mixdog-app-server-daemon compose_flip.rs: nothing to remove, no protocol method or service.

Not applicable: protocol rows, desktop wire, packaging.

For the follow-up task nr-office-pdf-jpx-decode (tier-1, dequantisation, inverse wavelet, component transforms):
   Codestream::tile(index) returns TileStructure whose CodeBlock carries numbps, passes, segments (passes, max_passes,
   len) and the concatenated data; Band carries orient, numbps, expn, mant and stepsize (OpenJPEG's value); the
   component parameters (CodingStyle: levels, cbw, cbh, style bits, reversible, precincts; Quant; roi_shift) are in
   TileStructure.params.comps; TileParams.mct and Siz.comps (precision, signed, dx, dy) complete what the decoder needs.
   Jp2Info gives colr, pclr, cmap and cdef (alpha_channels for SMaskInData).
